46:47.440 --> 46:48.440
Now, eat them.

46:48.440 --> 46:49.440
Swallow them.

46:49.440 --> 46:52.440
Swallow them.

46:52.440 --> 46:53.440
Thanks.

46:53.440 --> 47:02.440
Listen, I'm going to kick this guy's brains out.

47:02.440 --> 47:05.440
Well, adios.

47:05.440 --> 47:06.440
Bye.

47:06.440 --> 47:11.440
So you really were afraid of him.

47:11.440 --> 47:15.440
You're afraid of everybody that comes on this program.

47:15.440 --> 47:16.440
They all beat you up.

47:16.440 --> 47:17.440
I want to tell you something, Abbott.

47:17.440 --> 47:19.440
It's your whole fault, Lou.

47:19.440 --> 47:23.440
I was not afraid of Earl Flint tonight because Earl Flint was reading the script.

47:23.440 --> 47:24.440
Yeah, yeah.

47:24.440 --> 47:26.440
He was reading the script and he was supposed to be a tough guy.

47:26.440 --> 47:27.440
Yes, I'm still afraid of him.

47:27.440 --> 47:30.440
Now, if I had George Raft in Earl Flint's part...

47:30.440 --> 47:31.440
You had him here before.

47:31.440 --> 47:33.440
I would tell Raft off.

47:33.440 --> 47:44.440
I would smush him.

47:44.440 --> 47:47.440
I didn't think I read it that good.

47:47.440 --> 47:50.440
If Raft was here, I know what I would do.

47:50.440 --> 47:52.440
I would slug him all over the joint.

47:52.440 --> 47:56.440
Five weeks ago, he liked to kill me, in case you don't know it.

47:56.440 --> 47:57.440
I know it.

47:57.440 --> 48:00.440
If he was here right now, I would take this pistol.

48:00.440 --> 48:05.440
I would haul off and come down and hit him right on his head.

48:05.440 --> 48:12.440
And George, he would take the pistol and then the head and the hoo-hoo.

48:12.440 --> 48:15.440
And then the hoo-hoo.

48:15.440 --> 48:21.440
I lose more guns.

48:21.440 --> 48:22.440
I would...

48:22.440 --> 48:25.440
Give me that gun.

48:25.440 --> 48:27.440
George Raft.

48:27.440 --> 48:28.440
I would...

48:28.440 --> 48:29.440
George Raft.

48:29.440 --> 48:47.440
I would kill you, okay?

48:47.440 --> 48:56.440
Ah, he's perfectly all right.

48:56.440 --> 48:57.440
Well, friends.

48:57.440 --> 49:00.440
Ladies and gentlemen, we want to thank Earl Flint.

49:00.440 --> 49:02.440
We want to thank Rhonda Fleming.

49:02.440 --> 49:04.440
We want to thank Bruce Carpenter, most of all.

49:04.440 --> 49:09.440
We want to thank George Raft for coming down here tonight to sort of give us a surprise finish to the show.

49:09.440 --> 49:10.440
I want to thank you too, bud.

49:10.440 --> 49:11.440
I want to thank you.

49:11.440 --> 49:12.440
You were superb.

49:12.440 --> 49:13.440
Thank you.

49:13.440 --> 49:15.440
Now, we have...

49:15.440 --> 49:16.440
What is this?

49:16.440 --> 49:17.440
Mr. Raft.

49:17.440 --> 49:21.440
Thank you, Mr. Raft.

49:21.440 --> 49:23.440
The reason I came down...

49:23.440 --> 49:27.440
The Motion Picture Academy asked me to award this to Abbott and Costello.

49:27.440 --> 49:32.440
They said that you two fellas sell more corn and popcorn in the theaters

49:32.440 --> 49:38.440
while your picture is playing than any other picture that's ever been shown at the local theaters all over the world.

49:38.440 --> 49:41.440
And they said there's more corn in you two fellas than they've ever seen in their life.

49:41.440 --> 49:42.440
George, you know what it says there?

49:42.440 --> 49:46.440
It says the PopScar, this PopScar salesman.

49:46.440 --> 49:49.440
In other words, we sell more popcorn in theaters than anybody else.

49:49.440 --> 49:51.440
That's a nice trophy.

49:51.440 --> 49:52.440
That's a nice trophy.

49:52.440 --> 49:54.440
How are we going to break this in half though?

49:54.440 --> 49:56.440
Well, I'll tell you what I'll do, bud.

49:56.440 --> 50:00.440
I will present it to you because you have a wonderful den and it looks pretty in your den.

50:00.440 --> 50:01.440
Well, thanks a lot, George.

50:01.440 --> 50:04.440
For a week, then I'll come up and take it to my dad.

50:04.440 --> 50:05.440
That's what I thought.

50:05.440 --> 50:07.440
George, we want to thank you for coming down.

50:07.440 --> 50:08.440
Thanks a lot, George.

50:08.440 --> 50:09.440
I...

50:09.440 --> 50:14.440
Thank you all.

50:14.440 --> 50:17.440
I feel sort of a breeze back here.

50:17.440 --> 50:18.440
Why?

50:18.440 --> 50:19.440
I want to thank everybody.

50:19.440 --> 50:22.440
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen, for having us in your homes.

50:22.440 --> 50:23.440
Thank you for coming.

50:23.440 --> 50:24.440
Thank you all.

50:24.440 --> 50:25.440
I think that just about does it, I hope.

50:25.440 --> 50:26.440
Is it true?

50:26.440 --> 50:27.440
Is it right?

50:27.440 --> 50:28.440
Right.

50:28.440 --> 50:49.440
Thank you.

